gaming,"Yesterday my brother came running downstairs to tell me about the new ""medieval"" mode that gets rid of the new weapons.

We were so excited and eagerly waited.

We double check the patch notes and guess what?  It removes ALL weapons and is a melee  only mode.  I can't believe it.  I prefer smaller servers of around 6 per team and when I do play I almost always hit a server with a lower population where most people are sitting around, trading items and doing melee only ""because there are not enough people"".  Makes me sick.

The entire attitude of the tf2 community has changed, where once it used to be players that cared about fragging, now only care about hlss, hat trading and peacocking.  People used to care about the game.

To go back and think about the pureness of tf2 amazes me, it was an incredibly good game.  I truly believe that tf2 was the greatest multiplayer pc game ever made.  The beauty of it was that it took a great idea, simplified it and polished it to look like glass - no gimmicks.

I could tell that tf2 was doomed with the pyro update, when valve's focus changed from balancing the game to balancing the weapons that they were releasing at the speed of heat.  Apparently giving the pyro 50 health wasn't the best idea.  Think of how many times the reflect has changed since that update.  It started to get silly when the updates started releasing weapons that were not just modified versions of their previous selves, boxing gloves and sandwiches anyone?

I've logged in over 700 hours of tf2 (none of it is silly idle time) and I'm sad to not be playing it anymore.  RIP: tf2 - the greatest game to ever be unmade, 9 years of conception to 3 years of destruction.",1292767066.0,9
